1
00:00:01,320 --> 00:00:02,920
All depicted events are fictional

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,120
and for entertainment purposes only.
Viewer discretion is advised.

3
00:00:56,360 --> 00:00:58,280
Do you remember that shop still?

4
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:01,320
We should choose new rings to wear.

5
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:28,800
Run! Now!

6
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:34,240
Make way! Hurry!

7
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:41,240
Klao! Move!

8
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:43,800
Klao! This way!

9
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:03,560
We can go no further.

10
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:05,760
You must hide here.

11
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:08,280
I shall go and seize him myself.

12
00:02:09,039 --> 00:02:10,440
No, please!

13
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:13,400
What if we should be parted again?

14
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:15,640
Countless times have we been parted,

15
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:17,720
yet ever do I find my way to you.

16
00:02:22,680 --> 00:02:23,840
I promise you,

17
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:26,840
I shall return.

18
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:30,160
Nothing shall ever part us again.

19
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:15,200
Happy birthday, Nakun!

20
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:21,240
DECEMBER 2023

21
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:27,120
We're so sorry.

22
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:47,040
Gosh, Pun.

23
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:49,280
I thought Nakun was already at the shop?

24
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:50,880
The surprise is ruined.

25
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:54,760
He really said he was.

26
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:57,680
I have no idea why he's not here.

27
00:03:57,760 --> 00:03:58,720
That's okay.

28
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:00,040
We'll try again.

29
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:02,560
Guys, do we still have any party poppers?

30
00:04:02,640 --> 00:04:03,960
We're out.

31
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:06,120
He told me to pop them all at once.

32
00:04:07,760 --> 00:04:09,000
What do we do now?

33
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:10,200
Surprise.

34
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:29,320
Damn.

35
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:30,640
What the hell did you do?

36
00:04:35,160 --> 00:04:36,200
I'm all right!

37
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:44,080
Damn!

38
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:45,800
The state you're in…

39
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:47,880
Why do you look so bad?

40
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:50,320
-Thee!
-What?

41
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:51,920
Stop making fun of Nakun.

42
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,960
I'm not.

43
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:56,840
He's really forsaken by the heavens.

44
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,440
Taxis refused to take him,

45
00:04:59,520 --> 00:05:00,960
so he had to walk here.

46
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:02,280
Then the umbrella broke,

47
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:04,520
and a motorcycle
splashed him as it drove by.

48
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:05,840
When he finally got here,

49
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:08,680
he even stepped in some mud.

50
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:12,360
Bangkok…

51
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:15,240
A city of life…

52
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:24,920
It's okay, buddy.

53
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,200
Shake it off. Don't mind it.

54
00:05:27,280 --> 00:05:30,040
It's your birthday after all.
Make a wish, buddy.

55
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:55,600
Nakun…

56
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:05,280
Why do things always get in my way?

57
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:20,160
Happy birthday, Nakun.

58
00:06:20,240 --> 00:06:21,080
Thanks a lot.

59
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:22,680
Wishing you a ton of happiness.

60
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:25,600
So have you…

61
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:27,000
made a wish again?

62
00:06:28,200 --> 00:06:29,040
Yes, I have.

63
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:31,560
-What did you wish for?
-Why do you want to know?

64
00:06:31,640 --> 00:06:34,640
That way I'll know
if I should wish you well or not.

65
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:37,680
Do you really have to choose
what kind of wish to give?

66
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:39,680
I want him to find a great partner

67
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:41,120
so he's finally settled.

68
00:06:42,600 --> 00:06:44,080
Better wish that for yourself.

69
00:06:44,880 --> 00:06:46,720
I'm not officially taken,

70
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:49,840
but I've already found myself a good love.

71
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:55,160
Are you sure?

72
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:57,040
Of course I am.

73
00:06:57,920 --> 00:07:00,880
Even though you haven't chosen me yet,

74
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:03,320
my love for you

75
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:05,880
is surely a good thing for you.

76
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:09,560
I need to use the toilet.

77
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:11,360
To relieve yourself?

78
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:13,400
To throw up!

79
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:17,680
Pun, I'll help you rub your back.

80
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:27,640
MOM

81
00:07:38,160 --> 00:07:39,880
-I'll help.
-I'm so sorry.

82
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:41,800
-I'll help clean it up.
-It's okay.

83
00:07:41,880 --> 00:07:43,200
-It's fine.
-It's okay.

84
00:07:52,080 --> 00:07:52,920
Ow…

85
00:07:56,880 --> 00:07:57,880
Blood!

86
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:01,080
Shit! My phone!

87
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:04,600
The screen's totally cracked!

88
00:08:20,360 --> 00:08:21,720
So damn unlucky.

89
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:25,040
Can it be fixed, Nakun?

90
00:08:25,120 --> 00:08:26,960
You'd be better off getting a new one.

91
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:28,200
I can't.

92
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:30,240
No modeling gigs are coming up.

93
00:08:31,280 --> 00:08:32,840
I do think I'm handsome though…

94
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:36,360
-Bird poop!
-Nakun

95
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:37,640
Bird pooped on your head!

96
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:38,559
Nakun!

97
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:40,240
-That's a lot.
-Give me a moment.

98
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:41,640
Pun, wipe it off my head!

99
00:08:46,040 --> 00:08:47,320
Get it off my head!

100
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:49,720
Wipe it off my head!

101
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:51,160
-Get it off!
-Please wait.

102
00:08:59,240 --> 00:09:01,360
How can someone be this unlucky?

103
00:09:01,440 --> 00:09:03,080
Gosh, you're so unlucky!

104
00:09:03,880 --> 00:09:05,080
At least it's gone.

105
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:08,040
-Not like this!
-Just as you requested.

106
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:23,560
ONE MONTH LATER

107
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:51,680
Help me! Somebody!

108
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:53,880
Help! Someone just stole my handbag!

109
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:57,280
Help me!

110
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:58,600
Please help!

111
00:09:58,680 --> 00:10:00,760
That guy!
Help me catch the thief, please!

112
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:01,960
-Help me, please!
-Sure.

113
00:10:02,480 --> 00:10:03,720
Please! Catch that guy!

114
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:08,600
Stop!

115
00:10:10,760 --> 00:10:12,840
-Stop!
-Somebody, please catch the thief!

116
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:14,640
Catch him, please!

117
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:15,600
Hey, stop!

118
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:26,440
Stop running away already!

119
00:10:28,040 --> 00:10:29,040
Hey!

120
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:31,360
Let go.

121
00:10:32,280 --> 00:10:33,720
You're a thief, yet so slow.

122
00:10:36,280 --> 00:10:37,920
Give the handbag back to her.

123
00:10:38,560 --> 00:10:39,680
If she presses charges,

124
00:10:39,760 --> 00:10:41,880
you'll end up in jail
with a criminal record!

125
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:43,320
Hey, man…

126
00:10:43,400 --> 00:10:44,800
What do you want from me?

127
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:46,960
Please let me go.

128
00:10:47,040 --> 00:10:48,200
My mom's sick.

129
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:50,640
This money's for her.

130
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:53,520
Listen to me.

131
00:10:55,160 --> 00:10:57,080
To be human is to fight.

132
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:00,640
But don't fight others.

133
00:11:02,720 --> 00:11:04,000
You're still young

134
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:07,520
with a bright future ahead.

135
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:10,560
It's not too late to change your mind.

136
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:12,360
It's that person.

137
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:13,280
-That guy!
-Stop!

138
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:14,320
What the hell?

139
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:15,480
That's my handbag.

140
00:11:15,560 --> 00:11:16,720
That's mine.

141
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:18,720
You're a thief, yet you're so slow.

142
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:19,920
If she presses charges,

143
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:22,120
you'll end up in jail
with a criminal record.

144
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:26,160
Please listen to me. So…

145
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:28,920
To be human is to fight.

146
00:11:29,640 --> 00:11:30,920
But don't fight me.

147
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:33,120
Guys, listen to me.

148
00:11:33,200 --> 00:11:35,520
I fucking… Sorry.
I didn't--

149
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:41,000
Just believe me.

150
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,880
I think it's getting worse and worse.

151
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:45,320
This isn't normal.

152
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:47,120
So what?

153
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:48,560
Like I can change anything.

154
00:11:48,640 --> 00:11:50,160
Of course you can.

155
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:51,680
That's why I brought you here.

156
00:11:59,440 --> 00:12:01,960
FORTUNE TELLER RATTIKARN'S PAVILION

157
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,080
Are you crazy?

158
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:07,080
No thanks.

159
00:12:07,160 --> 00:12:08,440
-I'm leaving.
-Hold on!

160
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:10,480
The fortune teller here is really good.

161
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:12,400
Take my mom's word for it.

162
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:13,920
If it doesn't work out,

163
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,000
you can just go home,

164
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:16,160
okay?

165
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:23,680
Give it a try, Nakun.

166
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:26,880
If this is a scam, we'll leave.

167
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:32,360
Things like this are always a scam.

168
00:12:43,520 --> 00:12:44,680
Do you believe me now?

169
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:45,880
This is the real deal.

170
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:49,400
No.

171
00:12:49,480 --> 00:12:51,640
No matter how bad things get,
I'll never…

172
00:12:55,360 --> 00:12:57,080
So cold!

173
00:12:58,480 --> 00:13:01,240
How many times do I have to get soaked?

174
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:05,920
Come on, the water is warm.

175
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:07,960
I don't buy it.

176
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:10,280
You forced me here,
and now you're mocking me?

177
00:13:13,640 --> 00:13:14,840
The water really is warm.

178
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:15,760
It's hot, even.

179
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:18,720
One misfortune after another.

180
00:13:18,800 --> 00:13:21,000
If holy water makes you shiver,

181
00:13:21,080 --> 00:13:22,640
then it's no surprise.

182
00:13:25,120 --> 00:13:26,320
Ow!

183
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:33,200
Once you get changed,

184
00:13:33,280 --> 00:13:34,440
head inside.

185
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:37,200
We have a lot to talk about.

186
00:13:44,800 --> 00:13:45,840
Hey.

187
00:13:47,680 --> 00:13:51,320
How did you like the warm bath service?

188
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:53,320
-Try it yourself.
-Wait, wait.

189
00:13:55,280 --> 00:13:56,240
Out of the way!

190
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:59,280
-Looking good, Nakun.
-That's enough, Thee.

191
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:00,560
Move.

192
00:14:00,640 --> 00:14:01,960
Hey, what the hell?

193
00:14:02,040 --> 00:14:03,560
Wait up, please!

194
00:14:15,320 --> 00:14:16,840
Don't leave just yet.

195
00:14:22,560 --> 00:14:24,520
What the hell is wrong with you?

196
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:34,320
Rahu transits the natal sign.

197
00:14:34,400 --> 00:14:36,440
You are about to experience misfortune.

198
00:14:37,320 --> 00:14:38,160
And?

199
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:41,240
An incident will occur…

200
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:42,720
No.

201
00:14:42,800 --> 00:14:44,120
It has already occurred

202
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:46,800
since your birthday last month.

203
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:48,760
How did she know?

204
00:14:50,120 --> 00:14:51,120
It's written here.

205
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:52,160
4 DECEMBER 2003

206
00:14:52,240 --> 00:14:53,960
His date of birth and everything.

207
00:14:54,040 --> 00:14:56,000
-We told her everything.
-At any rate…

208
00:14:56,680 --> 00:14:59,280
The reading I did was from his
natal chart.

209
00:14:59,920 --> 00:15:01,200
I truly mean well.

210
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:04,400
This misfortune is fatal.

211
00:15:06,520 --> 00:15:08,040
Be extremely careful.

212
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:10,560
I'm heading home.

213
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:19,600
What promise did you make, and to whom?

214
00:15:19,680 --> 00:15:22,160
Someone from the past
awaits its fulfillment.

215
00:15:23,680 --> 00:15:26,240
This gives me chills.
Who did you make a promise to?

216
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:28,600
No one. This is nonsense.

217
00:15:28,680 --> 00:15:32,240
-Nakun, this is a serious matter.
-If it is, why are you smiling?

218
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:36,880
Is there any way we can help him?

219
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:39,040
Hold him down!

220
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:40,680
-Let me go!
-Hey! Hey!

221
00:15:40,760 --> 00:15:42,200
-Let me go!
-Pun, help me!

222
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:44,200
I don't want to!

223
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:46,240
-Pun, help me!
-Let me go!

224
00:15:46,880 --> 00:15:48,160
Thee, don't!

225
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:49,120
Thee!

226
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:51,040
I told you to let me go!

227
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:52,840
Quite a fighter, aren't you?

228
00:16:16,520 --> 00:16:17,960
Thanks.

229
00:16:23,040 --> 00:16:23,880
As for you…

230
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:27,160
it may be wise to lift your old curse.

231
00:16:27,840 --> 00:16:28,680
Me?

232
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:30,840
Whoever you felt resentment toward,

233
00:16:31,640 --> 00:16:33,200
release the grudges you hold.

234
00:16:33,280 --> 00:16:34,960
This will break the cycle.

235
00:16:37,120 --> 00:16:38,120
And you…

236
00:16:39,640 --> 00:16:41,400
Visit your family if possible.

237
00:16:41,480 --> 00:16:43,360
Take care of your mom and dad.

238
00:16:43,440 --> 00:16:45,080
It will alleviate your misfortune.

239
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:47,120
I don't have a dad.

240
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:48,560
It's just a divorce.

241
00:16:49,280 --> 00:16:51,200
He didn't pass away or anything.

242
00:16:52,080 --> 00:16:53,520
He is still your father.

243
00:16:57,880 --> 00:16:59,080
And…

244
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:02,640
you're going back to Ayutthaya, right?

245
00:17:03,920 --> 00:17:05,240
Did you tell her that?

246
00:17:05,319 --> 00:17:06,560
No, I didn't.

247
00:17:06,640 --> 00:17:08,040
No idea what you're thinking.

248
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:13,240
I don't need to be told that.

249
00:17:13,319 --> 00:17:14,599
This Friday,

250
00:17:14,680 --> 00:17:16,359
your mom is going to call you.

251
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:21,040
At night,
don't forget to bathe in the moonlight.

252
00:17:21,119 --> 00:17:22,880
And wear this.

253
00:17:22,960 --> 00:17:24,359
No, I'm not wearing it.

254
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:26,760
Hey, Thee!

255
00:17:28,319 --> 00:17:29,840
You must not take it off.

256
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:37,400
It's no use trying.

257
00:17:39,880 --> 00:17:41,320
Keep it on.

258
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:49,480
Time travel literature

259
00:17:49,560 --> 00:17:52,840
is not just about
traveling into the future

260
00:17:52,920 --> 00:17:56,360
or back in time to change something.

261
00:17:56,440 --> 00:17:59,360
It questions whether time itself

262
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:02,160
is a phenomenon of nature…

263
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:04,080
HOW IS THIS IMPORTANT TO ME?

264
00:18:04,160 --> 00:18:06,520
…or merely an illusion created by humans.

265
00:18:08,440 --> 00:18:14,640
We may think time moves linearly,

266
00:18:14,720 --> 00:18:17,040
but in the world of
time travel literature,

267
00:18:18,120 --> 00:18:21,280
it is often portrayed as fragmented.

268
00:18:24,560 --> 00:18:27,160
It jumps back and forth,

269
00:18:27,240 --> 00:18:28,720
moving in circles,

270
00:18:29,680 --> 00:18:31,880
as if it were a dream

271
00:18:31,960 --> 00:18:34,520
or a memory.

272
00:18:36,040 --> 00:18:38,520
Why are you taking notes in English?

273
00:18:38,600 --> 00:18:40,680
I was going to ask for it.

274
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:42,080
This suggests that

275
00:18:42,600 --> 00:18:45,160
the concepts of past
and future lives might exist.

276
00:18:49,800 --> 00:18:51,000
Thee, give it back to me.

277
00:18:53,560 --> 00:18:54,840
Students over there…

278
00:18:58,680 --> 00:18:59,520
Yes, you.

279
00:19:03,760 --> 00:19:05,160
What's your name?

280
00:19:05,840 --> 00:19:06,720
She's asking you--

281
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:19,560
It's Khun,

282
00:19:21,120 --> 00:19:24,120
short for Nakun.

283
00:19:24,200 --> 00:19:26,080
"Khun, short for Nakun?"

284
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:28,560
That's a mouthful.

285
00:19:30,760 --> 00:19:34,320
You can call me Khun for short, Professor.

286
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:44,680
Do you believe in multiple lifetimes?

287
00:19:45,760 --> 00:19:47,360
Yeah, do you?

288
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:48,320
Answer her.

289
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:49,440
Do you?

290
00:19:49,920 --> 00:19:50,760
Come on.

291
00:19:52,040 --> 00:19:53,000
Answer the question.

292
00:19:53,080 --> 00:19:54,440
I don't.

293
00:19:59,200 --> 00:20:04,000
I think it's an idea created by humans

294
00:20:04,640 --> 00:20:06,560
to cope with loss

295
00:20:08,080 --> 00:20:10,560
or things they can't explain.

296
00:20:12,360 --> 00:20:13,480
Interesting.

297
00:20:13,560 --> 00:20:14,720
And?

298
00:20:14,800 --> 00:20:15,800
Well…

299
00:20:16,600 --> 00:20:18,440
Say, if we were born with hardships,

300
00:20:19,960 --> 00:20:23,120
we might say it's the consequence
of actions from a past life.

301
00:20:24,080 --> 00:20:26,480
Then tell ourselves to be content
with what we have

302
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:29,520
and to keep cultivating good deeds,

303
00:20:31,240 --> 00:20:34,400
without recognizing
the underlying social issues.

304
00:20:34,480 --> 00:20:35,400
Sheesh.

305
00:20:39,080 --> 00:20:41,480
I believe in logic.

306
00:20:41,560 --> 00:20:43,240
Every action

307
00:20:43,320 --> 00:20:45,400
has its consequences.

308
00:20:46,040 --> 00:20:47,400
But…

309
00:20:47,480 --> 00:20:50,840
I don't think consequences
carry over to our next lives.

310
00:20:52,360 --> 00:20:54,560
What an interesting answer.

311
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:58,440
Those who don't believe in
multiple lifetimes might think that

312
00:20:58,520 --> 00:21:04,040
we have the power to shape our own destiny

313
00:21:04,120 --> 00:21:07,400
and that nothing is predetermined,

314
00:21:07,480 --> 00:21:08,480
correct?

315
00:21:11,520 --> 00:21:12,640
Be careful, Nakun.

316
00:21:13,800 --> 00:21:17,360
In the world of time travel literature,

317
00:21:17,440 --> 00:21:21,120
we cannot always rely on logic.

318
00:21:22,880 --> 00:21:28,920
It might reflect something
that lies deep within.

319
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:32,400
It might be fear,

320
00:21:34,520 --> 00:21:35,720
hope,

321
00:21:35,800 --> 00:21:41,000
or the unwillingness
to believe in something,

322
00:21:41,720 --> 00:21:42,560
correct?

323
00:21:44,520 --> 00:21:45,520
Well, I…

324
00:21:46,160 --> 00:21:47,800
I have no fear, Professor.

325
00:21:51,800 --> 00:21:53,880
You have no fear?

326
00:21:53,960 --> 00:21:57,000
Be honest with yourself and ask

327
00:21:58,160 --> 00:22:01,040
whether you truly have no fear.

328
00:22:13,960 --> 00:22:14,800
Hey.

329
00:22:14,880 --> 00:22:16,080
Come on.

330
00:22:16,680 --> 00:22:17,520
Take it easy.

331
00:22:18,360 --> 00:22:19,240
Sit down.

332
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:39,800
Do you believe in multiple lifetimes?

333
00:22:39,880 --> 00:22:41,880
That's the topic of your assignment.

334
00:22:41,960 --> 00:22:44,640
Gosh!

335
00:22:44,720 --> 00:22:46,080
The deadline is today.

336
00:22:46,160 --> 00:22:47,760
No!

337
00:22:49,240 --> 00:22:50,440
Class dismissed.

338
00:22:51,480 --> 00:22:52,320
<i>Nakun.</i>

339
00:22:52,400 --> 00:22:56,360
Go take care of your mother,
as the fortune teller said.

340
00:22:56,440 --> 00:22:59,800
Having ill luck is bad enough,
yet you have doomed us all.

341
00:22:59,880 --> 00:23:01,480
That has nothing to do with me.

342
00:23:01,560 --> 00:23:04,400
Professors here love giving
piles of assignments.

343
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:08,360
Why did I have to get into this faculty?

344
00:23:11,520 --> 00:23:13,440
Can we go back in time and change this?

345
00:23:14,800 --> 00:23:15,720
Going back in time?

346
00:23:16,360 --> 00:23:17,280
See?

347
00:23:17,720 --> 00:23:20,320
The professor filled your head
with time-travel ideas.

348
00:23:21,200 --> 00:23:22,280
Yeah, you're right.

349
00:23:23,920 --> 00:23:24,840
But I'd rather not.

350
00:23:24,920 --> 00:23:28,640
If I studied at a different faculty,
I wouldn't get to see Pun.

351
00:23:29,320 --> 00:23:30,480
Has anyone told you that

352
00:23:31,520 --> 00:23:33,160
when you talk about Pun,

353
00:23:33,960 --> 00:23:35,680
you act like a Siberian Husky?

354
00:23:38,040 --> 00:23:39,120
Who said that?

355
00:23:39,200 --> 00:23:40,160
Was it Pun?

356
00:23:40,240 --> 00:23:41,080
Me.

357
00:23:43,280 --> 00:23:46,680
Pun is like a Persian cat though.

358
00:23:47,280 --> 00:23:49,920
Cats and dogs don't get along very well.

359
00:23:51,640 --> 00:23:54,480
But I've seen videos on TikTok.
They can be together.

360
00:23:55,200 --> 00:23:56,760
Stop talking nonsense.

361
00:24:00,040 --> 00:24:01,440
Yeah, what does this mean?

362
00:24:02,400 --> 00:24:04,360
Nakun… Nakun.

363
00:24:04,440 --> 00:24:05,680
Nakun!

364
00:24:09,200 --> 00:24:10,480
I'm returning your notes.

365
00:24:10,560 --> 00:24:11,880
Thanks to you,

366
00:24:11,960 --> 00:24:14,400
I got the top score
on the Western History exam.

367
00:24:14,480 --> 00:24:15,480
Thank you.

368
00:24:15,560 --> 00:24:17,040
You're amazing, Pun.

369
00:24:17,120 --> 00:24:19,560
Your fraternity brother
topped the class in English?

370
00:24:19,640 --> 00:24:21,920
But he's hopeless at Thai history.

371
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:24,000
Thee.

372
00:24:24,080 --> 00:24:26,200
What? The midterm exam was last week,

373
00:24:26,280 --> 00:24:28,480
and you said
you couldn't remember a thing.

374
00:24:28,560 --> 00:24:30,960
We're talking about Nakun here, you know?

375
00:24:31,040 --> 00:24:34,480
He was just being humble.
He'll get an A when the results come out.

376
00:24:34,560 --> 00:24:35,920
Yeah, you're right.

377
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:38,920
Nakun always says he hasn't studied
and can't do the exam,

378
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:41,320
but he's always at the top of the class.

379
00:24:46,080 --> 00:24:47,720
MOM

380
00:24:47,800 --> 00:24:50,360
<i>Nakun, are you coming home for the break?</i>

381
00:24:50,440 --> 00:24:51,680
<i>I miss you.</i>

382
00:24:51,760 --> 00:24:53,520
<i>We haven't celebrated your birthday.</i>

383
00:24:53,600 --> 00:24:55,640
<i>Give me a call once your classes are over.</i>

384
00:24:57,440 --> 00:25:00,000
By the way,
we studied time travel literature today.

385
00:25:00,080 --> 00:25:02,040
About multiple lifetimes.

386
00:25:03,280 --> 00:25:05,640
-Do you believe in that?
-Multiple lifetimes.

387
00:25:08,240 --> 00:25:09,640
I guess I do.

388
00:25:09,720 --> 00:25:12,560
The concept sounds fun
if you think about it.

389
00:25:12,640 --> 00:25:14,920
If you do, I will too.

390
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:18,760
Perhaps our paths
have crossed in past lives.

391
00:25:19,560 --> 00:25:21,480
Then we'll meet again in the next one.

392
00:25:21,560 --> 00:25:22,440
Okay.

393
00:25:23,440 --> 00:25:24,960
Then I don't believe in it.

394
00:25:25,040 --> 00:25:26,760
This lifetime is more than enough.

395
00:25:27,640 --> 00:25:29,760
What? Why?

396
00:25:29,840 --> 00:25:32,360
Souls only have so many lifetimes to meet.

397
00:25:32,440 --> 00:25:34,120
Can't I meet you in the next life?

398
00:25:34,200 --> 00:25:35,960
This lifetime is already killing me.

399
00:25:36,040 --> 00:25:36,920
Why?

400
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:38,000
-No.
-Pun, wait up!

401
00:25:38,080 --> 00:25:39,320
-Nope.
-What's the rush?

402
00:25:39,400 --> 00:25:41,720
-Why are you always on my case?
-Wait for me.

403
00:26:08,360 --> 00:26:09,560
<i>Be careful, Nakun.</i>

404
00:26:10,600 --> 00:26:14,120
In the world of time travel literature,

405
00:26:14,200 --> 00:26:17,920
we cannot always rely on logic.

406
00:26:18,880 --> 00:26:24,960
<i>It might reflect something</i>
<i>that lies deep within.</i>

407
00:26:33,040 --> 00:26:34,920
Be careful, Nakun.

408
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:39,000
-Hey! Nakun!
-Nakun!

409
00:26:41,120 --> 00:26:42,720
D.E. 6613
PHRA NAKHON SI AYUTTHAYA

410
00:26:42,800 --> 00:26:44,880
Are you okay? All good?

411
00:26:48,880 --> 00:26:49,800
It's okay.

412
00:26:50,840 --> 00:26:51,920
That really scared me.

413
00:27:06,120 --> 00:27:07,040
Hey, Nakun.

414
00:27:07,120 --> 00:27:08,040
Nakun!

415
00:27:08,120 --> 00:27:09,760
-Look out!
-Hey!

416
00:27:15,160 --> 00:27:16,000
Hey…

417
00:27:16,080 --> 00:27:17,400
-Shit…
-Nakun!

418
00:27:19,280 --> 00:27:20,240
Are you hurt?

419
00:27:20,320 --> 00:27:21,160
Damn…

420
00:27:22,760 --> 00:27:23,920
How did that fall over?

421
00:27:24,840 --> 00:27:25,920
Are you okay?

422
00:27:26,480 --> 00:27:28,040
Are you all right, Nakun?

423
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:32,520
<i>You're…</i>

424
00:27:32,600 --> 00:27:34,960
going back to Ayutthaya anyway,
aren't you?

425
00:27:35,040 --> 00:27:37,200
It just fell down randomly.

426
00:27:37,280 --> 00:27:39,880
D.E. 6613
PHRA NAKHON SI AYUTTHAYA

427
00:27:47,400 --> 00:27:48,560
Mom…

428
00:27:59,520 --> 00:28:01,640
CERTIFICATE OF EXCELLENCE
Nakun PHATTANATADA

429
00:28:14,760 --> 00:28:16,240
I'm finally home.

430
00:28:36,120 --> 00:28:37,040
Oh, Nakun?

431
00:28:37,120 --> 00:28:38,840
You're home late.

432
00:28:38,920 --> 00:28:40,960
Oh, Mom?

433
00:28:56,520 --> 00:28:58,920
You look amazing, ma'am.

434
00:28:59,000 --> 00:29:01,400
Your son just got home,
and you're leaving already?

435
00:29:01,480 --> 00:29:03,360
Oh, no, I'm not.

436
00:29:03,440 --> 00:29:06,000
I'm leaving for
the District Chief's child's wedding.

437
00:29:06,080 --> 00:29:07,560
Do you want to come with me?

438
00:29:07,640 --> 00:29:09,640
The party will last the whole night.

439
00:29:09,720 --> 00:29:10,800
I'll pass.

440
00:29:10,880 --> 00:29:12,520
District Chief's child?

441
00:29:12,600 --> 00:29:14,040
I don't even know their name.

442
00:29:15,560 --> 00:29:16,880
I thought so.

443
00:29:16,960 --> 00:29:21,520
But I've prepared dinner for you.

444
00:29:22,640 --> 00:29:24,080
Eat a lot of rice, all right?

445
00:29:24,160 --> 00:29:25,800
Don't just go for the main dishes.

446
00:29:33,240 --> 00:29:34,600
This much?

447
00:29:35,120 --> 00:29:37,680
Are you throwing a party or something?

448
00:29:37,760 --> 00:29:39,120
You'll finish all of that.

449
00:29:39,200 --> 00:29:40,920
If you're not full,

450
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:45,880
there is fruit and snacks in the fridge.

451
00:29:45,960 --> 00:29:48,120
Go ahead and go to town on them, got it?

452
00:29:48,200 --> 00:29:49,040
Sure…

453
00:29:50,200 --> 00:29:51,160
Do I look beautiful?

454
00:29:53,960 --> 00:29:54,920
I guess.

455
00:29:55,680 --> 00:29:57,680
I'll be going now.

456
00:30:03,040 --> 00:30:03,880
Nakun!

457
00:30:04,720 --> 00:30:05,560
Wait…

458
00:30:06,200 --> 00:30:07,680
What happened to your face?

459
00:30:10,440 --> 00:30:12,160
Oh, this?

460
00:30:13,720 --> 00:30:15,960
No one would dare hurt me, Mom.

461
00:30:16,720 --> 00:30:19,240
I fell over.

462
00:30:19,320 --> 00:30:21,760
And I ended up slamming my head!

463
00:30:21,840 --> 00:30:23,880
So my face got all swollen…

464
00:30:27,360 --> 00:30:28,480
Oh, for goodness' sake…

465
00:30:28,560 --> 00:30:31,240
So you were just being clumsy as usual.

466
00:30:31,320 --> 00:30:34,520
I thought you got into a fight
or something.

467
00:30:36,120 --> 00:30:38,280
Who would I even fight, Mom?

468
00:30:38,880 --> 00:30:42,320
You, the deputy,
have taught me since I was little

469
00:30:42,400 --> 00:30:44,200
that violence is off-limits.

470
00:30:45,600 --> 00:30:48,560
And when I do something,
make sure no one can criticize me.

471
00:30:48,640 --> 00:30:49,920
Isn't that right?

472
00:30:51,240 --> 00:30:52,720
I'm so proud of you, honey.

473
00:30:52,800 --> 00:30:54,120
That really warms my heart.

474
00:30:54,200 --> 00:30:56,400
Gosh! What's gotten into you?

475
00:30:56,480 --> 00:30:57,760
I'm overjoyed, okay?

476
00:30:57,840 --> 00:30:58,920
I'm proud of you.

477
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:01,680
Raising you on my own
into the good boy you are today

478
00:31:01,760 --> 00:31:03,160
makes me incredibly proud.

479
00:31:03,240 --> 00:31:04,120
One more.

480
00:31:07,680 --> 00:31:09,000
What is this?

481
00:31:10,840 --> 00:31:12,440
Why don't you head out already?

482
00:31:12,520 --> 00:31:14,640
Drinks don't pour themselves, you know.

483
00:31:15,360 --> 00:31:16,680
I don't drink.

484
00:31:18,880 --> 00:31:19,720
I'm off.

485
00:31:23,080 --> 00:31:24,000
Good luck.

486
00:31:24,640 --> 00:31:25,640
Thanks!

487
00:31:41,480 --> 00:31:43,200
And you said you don't drink…

488
00:31:47,480 --> 00:31:48,480
Well, then…

489
00:31:49,400 --> 00:31:50,680
If she doesn't drink,

490
00:31:53,440 --> 00:31:54,640
then this is all mine.

491
00:31:58,600 --> 00:32:00,760
DETECTIVE CONAN

492
00:32:26,760 --> 00:32:28,560
DO YOU BELIEVE IN MULTIPLE LIFETIMES?

493
00:32:28,640 --> 00:32:29,520
I FREAKING DON'T!

494
00:32:42,360 --> 00:32:44,680
"Thai History Test Results."

495
00:32:45,240 --> 00:32:47,480
Why did the results come out so early?

496
00:32:49,520 --> 00:32:51,440
"Mr. Nakun Pattanatada"

497
00:32:53,120 --> 00:32:54,000
I got…

498
00:32:54,680 --> 00:32:57,680
fourteen and a half.

499
00:33:19,400 --> 00:33:21,400
First time failing an exam.

500
00:33:22,920 --> 00:33:25,360
Am I really suffering from misfortune?

501
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:43,920
Geese.

502
00:33:44,000 --> 00:33:45,560
Geese, where are you guys?

503
00:33:46,760 --> 00:33:47,640
Geese!

504
00:33:48,720 --> 00:33:50,480
Come out, it's feeding time.

505
00:33:51,800 --> 00:33:52,920
Where are they?

506
00:34:00,920 --> 00:34:02,160
Oh, I missed the bucket.

507
00:34:05,040 --> 00:34:07,120
Come and feed yourselves then.

508
00:34:13,440 --> 00:34:14,920
It's always me!

509
00:34:15,000 --> 00:34:17,120
It always happens to me!

510
00:34:18,920 --> 00:34:22,760
Why does a future honors English student
have to fail Thai History!

511
00:34:23,880 --> 00:34:25,400
If past lives do exist,

512
00:34:25,480 --> 00:34:28,280
why aren't my past memories
carried over into this life

513
00:34:28,360 --> 00:34:30,880
so I don't have to study Thai History!

514
00:34:30,960 --> 00:34:31,800
Gosh!

515
00:34:35,639 --> 00:34:37,239
Might as well take a swig…

516
00:34:49,920 --> 00:34:51,239
Gorgeous.

517
00:34:54,199 --> 00:34:55,840
Look…

518
00:34:55,920 --> 00:34:57,720
Even a star is falling on me.

519
00:35:08,920 --> 00:35:10,280
Is it actually falling?

520
00:35:31,240 --> 00:35:32,280
Ow…

521
00:35:49,000 --> 00:35:50,600
Master Klao is over there!

522
00:35:51,480 --> 00:35:53,840
Tread lightly!
There are king cobra dens.

523
00:35:56,920 --> 00:35:57,800
Master Klao.

524
00:35:57,880 --> 00:35:58,840
Master.

525
00:35:58,920 --> 00:35:59,760
Master Klao!

526
00:35:59,840 --> 00:36:00,720
-What?
-Master!

527
00:36:00,800 --> 00:36:02,040
Master Klao.

528
00:36:02,840 --> 00:36:03,760
-What?
-Master Klao!

529
00:36:04,760 --> 00:36:05,760
-Master Klao.
-Master.

530
00:36:05,840 --> 00:36:07,400
-Master Klao!
-Gosh! Who are you?

531
00:36:09,080 --> 00:36:10,240
-Ow! That hurt!
-Master.

532
00:36:10,920 --> 00:36:12,240
His Excellency and the Lord

533
00:36:12,320 --> 00:36:14,640
commanded us
to search for you several days.

534
00:36:15,440 --> 00:36:17,480
What circumstances led you to these woods?

535
00:36:25,880 --> 00:36:27,480
Master?

536
00:36:27,560 --> 00:36:28,480
What the hell?

537
00:36:40,480 --> 00:36:42,280
<i>-Bastard!</i>
<i>-You son of a rogue!</i>

538
00:36:43,440 --> 00:36:45,680
<i>Father and son alike, wretched both!</i>

539
00:36:47,360 --> 00:36:48,280
<i>Scum!</i>

540
00:36:48,360 --> 00:36:50,720
<i>The likes of you shall never</i>
<i>prosper, Klao!</i>

541
00:36:50,800 --> 00:36:53,680
<i>The likes of you shall never</i>
<i>prosper, Klao!</i>

542
00:36:53,760 --> 00:36:55,440
Does your head hurt?

543
00:36:55,520 --> 00:36:58,360
Everyone! Escort him back
to His Excellency's estate.

544
00:36:58,440 --> 00:36:59,720
Master Klao!

545
00:36:59,800 --> 00:37:00,720
My Master!

546
00:37:00,800 --> 00:37:01,640
Master Klao!

547
00:37:01,720 --> 00:37:02,800
Master!

548
00:37:02,880 --> 00:37:04,760
My Master!

549
00:37:04,840 --> 00:37:05,720
What a comfort!

550
00:37:05,800 --> 00:37:07,120
You are still alive?

551
00:37:07,200 --> 00:37:08,840
-How are you, Master?
-Hey!

552
00:37:10,600 --> 00:37:13,520
Who are you guys?

553
00:37:14,280 --> 00:37:15,520
And I'm…

554
00:37:17,280 --> 00:37:18,720
I'm not dreaming, am I?

555
00:37:21,040 --> 00:37:22,400
I beg your pardon?

556
00:37:26,080 --> 00:37:27,240
You've got it all wrong.

557
00:37:27,320 --> 00:37:28,160
I'm not Klao.

558
00:37:28,240 --> 00:37:29,640
Oh, Master.

559
00:37:29,720 --> 00:37:31,520
You still jest at a time like this.

560
00:37:31,600 --> 00:37:33,520
This suggests that you are well.

561
00:37:33,600 --> 00:37:34,760
Is it not so?

562
00:37:34,840 --> 00:37:36,200
You…

563
00:37:43,120 --> 00:37:45,320
You're filming a period piece,
aren't you?

564
00:37:45,400 --> 00:37:48,640
Since when has my mom
let people film a play in her orchard?

565
00:37:50,880 --> 00:37:51,720
Film…

566
00:37:54,960 --> 00:37:56,040
A play?

567
00:37:57,840 --> 00:37:59,160
A play…

568
00:37:59,240 --> 00:38:00,080
You…

569
00:38:00,160 --> 00:38:02,040
What are you doing? Filming content?

570
00:38:05,360 --> 00:38:06,240
Master Klao…

571
00:38:10,760 --> 00:38:11,600
Wait…

572
00:38:12,240 --> 00:38:13,880
This is different from last night.

573
00:38:14,360 --> 00:38:15,840
What is this place?

574
00:38:24,320 --> 00:38:26,320
Last night, I was drinking.

575
00:38:28,960 --> 00:38:30,840
After that, I left the house.

576
00:38:31,920 --> 00:38:33,440
And then, the star fell!

577
00:38:35,840 --> 00:38:37,320
Then I ended up here.

578
00:38:39,520 --> 00:38:40,600
What's next?

579
00:38:41,480 --> 00:38:44,280
God! I was too drunk to remember anything!

580
00:38:44,360 --> 00:38:45,840
I too have been pondering

581
00:38:45,920 --> 00:38:48,040
the circumstances that brought you here.

582
00:38:48,120 --> 00:38:50,120
-My Lord…
-My Lord.

583
00:39:21,680 --> 00:39:22,960
Who's that?

584
00:39:23,040 --> 00:39:24,360
He looks so familiar.

585
00:39:24,440 --> 00:39:25,520
A celebrity?

586
00:39:27,360 --> 00:39:28,520
How is that?

587
00:39:29,480 --> 00:39:31,000
Will you now tell me?

588
00:39:35,440 --> 00:39:37,120
I think you've got it all wrong.

589
00:39:37,200 --> 00:39:39,360
I'm not an actor.

590
00:39:39,440 --> 00:39:42,800
I'm Nahathai's son,

591
00:39:44,120 --> 00:39:46,440
from the nearby mango orchard.

592
00:39:46,520 --> 00:39:49,360
Last night, I must've gotten pretty drunk,

593
00:39:49,440 --> 00:39:51,920
wandered around, and ended up here.

594
00:39:53,200 --> 00:39:55,720
That said,
I won't trouble you any further.

595
00:39:55,800 --> 00:39:56,720
Take care, guys.

596
00:39:57,360 --> 00:39:58,200
Seize him!

597
00:39:58,280 --> 00:40:00,720
-Don't let him out of our sight.
-What the hell?

598
00:40:01,240 --> 00:40:02,480
Hey, let go of me!

599
00:40:02,560 --> 00:40:03,400
You…

600
00:40:04,200 --> 00:40:05,560
This course of action…

601
00:40:05,640 --> 00:40:07,320
I could sue you for this!

602
00:40:11,360 --> 00:40:12,840
Master Klao! Master!

603
00:40:12,920 --> 00:40:14,200
Master! Master Klao!

604
00:40:14,280 --> 00:40:15,120
Master Klao!

605
00:40:20,440 --> 00:40:21,520
My Lord!

606
00:40:21,600 --> 00:40:23,440
I beg you,
please spare him the cane.

607
00:40:23,520 --> 00:40:24,720
The fault is mine alone.

608
00:40:24,840 --> 00:40:26,760
You entrusted Master Klao to me,

609
00:40:26,840 --> 00:40:30,040
yet I have failed you
by permitting him to indulge in spirits.

610
00:40:30,120 --> 00:40:31,480
Enough!

611
00:40:32,160 --> 00:40:33,800
No one shall be punished.

612
00:40:34,680 --> 00:40:36,600
Attend to your master at once,

613
00:40:36,680 --> 00:40:38,280
and bring him to the small manor.

614
00:40:39,800 --> 00:40:41,280
Not to His Excellency's estate?

615
00:40:41,960 --> 00:40:43,120
Not at this moment.

616
00:40:43,200 --> 00:40:44,360
Is it not evident

617
00:40:44,440 --> 00:40:47,040
that your master is troubled in mind?

618
00:40:47,120 --> 00:40:49,080
I wish to spare my parents from distress.

619
00:40:50,520 --> 00:40:51,360
Yes, my Lord.

620
00:40:52,280 --> 00:40:53,280
Waste no time.

621
00:40:54,320 --> 00:40:55,600
Find Klao at once.

622
00:40:56,400 --> 00:40:57,960
I shall follow shortly after.

623
00:40:59,040 --> 00:41:00,080
Yes, my Lord.

624
00:41:01,120 --> 00:41:02,240
Master Klao!

625
00:41:03,000 --> 00:41:03,840
Master Klao!

626
00:41:03,920 --> 00:41:04,880
Master!

627
00:41:04,960 --> 00:41:06,200
Master Klao! Master!

628
00:41:06,280 --> 00:41:08,200
-Master!
-Master Klao!

629
00:41:10,120 --> 00:41:11,320
Let go of me!

630
00:41:12,000 --> 00:41:13,280
-Master…
-Let me go!

631
00:41:13,360 --> 00:41:15,120
Let go!

632
00:41:15,200 --> 00:41:16,360
Ow!

633
00:41:16,440 --> 00:41:18,240
I told you to let go of me! Come on!

634
00:41:19,080 --> 00:41:20,720
You've got the wrong person!

635
00:41:20,800 --> 00:41:22,080
Please, Master.

636
00:41:24,680 --> 00:41:25,960
Master, please.

637
00:41:26,040 --> 00:41:27,840
I'll sue! I'll sue!

638
00:41:27,920 --> 00:41:28,760
My phone.

639
00:41:29,600 --> 00:41:31,400
You even took my phone from me!

640
00:41:32,480 --> 00:41:33,520
-Master Klao.
-Gosh!

641
00:41:33,600 --> 00:41:35,400
Not going anywhere!

642
00:41:38,240 --> 00:41:40,200
Let me go!

643
00:41:40,280 --> 00:41:41,360
Let go!

644
00:41:41,880 --> 00:41:43,600
Help! Somebody, help!

645
00:41:44,280 --> 00:41:45,160
This way, Master.

646
00:41:45,240 --> 00:41:46,160
Gentle, please!

647
00:42:02,120 --> 00:42:03,720
Where am I now?

648
00:42:03,800 --> 00:42:06,720
Lord Phop arranged
these quarters for your comfort.

649
00:42:07,760 --> 00:42:08,600
Lord?

650
00:42:09,800 --> 00:42:12,120
You mean the guy
with the scary-looking face?

651
00:42:13,600 --> 00:42:15,720
Please cease this mockery, Master Klao.

652
00:42:15,800 --> 00:42:18,160
My heart grows uneasy.

653
00:42:18,240 --> 00:42:20,040
You need to stop playing games.

654
00:42:21,280 --> 00:42:22,920
I'm not entertained by this.

655
00:42:23,000 --> 00:42:23,920
It actually hurt.

656
00:42:26,080 --> 00:42:28,480
You dragged me
to a cabin in the middle of nowhere.

657
00:42:32,240 --> 00:42:34,280
"Cabin in the middle of nowhere"?

658
00:42:36,040 --> 00:42:37,920
This is kidnapping.

659
00:42:38,880 --> 00:42:41,040
I'll take this matter all the way.

660
00:42:41,120 --> 00:42:43,520
Also, tell the "Lord," or whoever he is,

661
00:42:43,600 --> 00:42:45,560
to be ready to face me in court.

662
00:42:53,520 --> 00:42:54,520
Master.

663
00:42:55,200 --> 00:42:57,520
How may I, Chuay,

664
00:42:57,600 --> 00:42:58,960
be of service to you?

665
00:42:59,040 --> 00:43:00,120
Your name's Chuay?

666
00:43:01,360 --> 00:43:02,760
Master…

667
00:43:04,160 --> 00:43:05,760
Even I, you…

668
00:43:12,360 --> 00:43:13,360
It's hot in here.

669
00:43:13,440 --> 00:43:15,320
Can you turn on the AC, Chuay?

670
00:43:17,360 --> 00:43:18,440
The AC.

671
00:43:21,240 --> 00:43:22,080
Turn on…

672
00:43:22,160 --> 00:43:23,280
the A…

673
00:43:27,600 --> 00:43:29,280
Don't tell me there's no AC here.

674
00:43:30,640 --> 00:43:33,120
Grant this humble servant
your pardon, Master.

675
00:43:35,000 --> 00:43:36,880
Stop calling me Klao already.

676
00:43:36,960 --> 00:43:38,160
My name is not Klao!

677
00:43:38,920 --> 00:43:39,920
Master Klao…

678
00:43:40,880 --> 00:43:41,720
Waste of time.

679
00:43:42,720 --> 00:43:44,240
No, Master!

680
00:43:44,320 --> 00:43:46,520
The Lord requested
that you seek repose here.

681
00:43:46,600 --> 00:43:47,760
Should you leave,

682
00:43:47,840 --> 00:43:49,440
I shall receive a harsh caning.

683
00:43:50,960 --> 00:43:53,000
Stop playing
the character for a second?

684
00:43:55,040 --> 00:43:56,240
Playing the character?

685
00:43:58,160 --> 00:44:00,360
I lack the talent.
I have not mastered the art.

686
00:44:01,360 --> 00:44:03,320
You keep up your character so well.

687
00:44:03,400 --> 00:44:05,000
Where did you learn to act?

688
00:44:05,080 --> 00:44:08,640
You are well aware that
I'm no master of <i>Farangi</i> speech.

689
00:44:10,480 --> 00:44:11,400
What speech?

690
00:44:11,480 --> 00:44:13,320
<i>"Farangi,"</i> Master.

691
00:44:14,160 --> 00:44:15,880
<i>"Farangi"?</i>

692
00:44:16,560 --> 00:44:17,960
Like, French?

693
00:44:18,040 --> 00:44:19,400
I was speaking English.

694
00:44:20,360 --> 00:44:22,120
<i>"Fa-ran-gi,"</i> Master.

695
00:44:23,240 --> 00:44:24,440
Who cares.

696
00:44:25,200 --> 00:44:26,200
Listen.

697
00:44:26,280 --> 00:44:28,400
I don't know what you're trying to do,

698
00:44:28,480 --> 00:44:31,640
maybe make a screenplay,
kidnap me for ransom,

699
00:44:31,720 --> 00:44:33,120
or something,

700
00:44:33,680 --> 00:44:35,680
but you've got the wrong guy.

701
00:44:35,760 --> 00:44:37,360
My name is not Klao.

702
00:44:37,440 --> 00:44:39,080
It's Nakun.

703
00:44:39,160 --> 00:44:41,760
Also, I'm useless to you.

704
00:44:41,840 --> 00:44:44,480
My mom definitely doesn't have
money for a ransom.

705
00:44:50,760 --> 00:44:51,760
Chuay.

706
00:44:52,760 --> 00:44:54,280
You look like a good person.

707
00:44:56,560 --> 00:44:59,360
Can you please let me go?

708
00:45:01,160 --> 00:45:02,160
I won't snitch.

709
00:45:15,200 --> 00:45:16,360
Master! Wait!

710
00:45:23,120 --> 00:45:24,880
Where do you wander to now, Klao?

711
00:45:26,200 --> 00:45:27,560
I'm getting out of here.

712
00:45:27,640 --> 00:45:28,960
Move.

713
00:45:29,720 --> 00:45:31,080
You are attired oddly.

714
00:45:33,040 --> 00:45:34,720
Hey, what are you doing?

715
00:45:34,800 --> 00:45:35,880
Stop it.

716
00:45:35,960 --> 00:45:37,920
The butterfly-shaped mark of birth.

717
00:45:38,000 --> 00:45:39,840
There is no mistaking you, Klao.

718
00:45:41,800 --> 00:45:42,960
Butterfly-shaped?

719
00:45:43,040 --> 00:45:45,080
It's shaped like northern Thailand.

720
00:45:45,160 --> 00:45:46,840
Have your wits forsaken you?

721
00:45:46,920 --> 00:45:49,040
Is it overindulgence
that clouds your words?

722
00:45:49,120 --> 00:45:51,000
I'm the one speaking coherently.

723
00:45:52,720 --> 00:45:55,760
I had a little too much drink last night,
but I wasn't out cold.

724
00:45:59,000 --> 00:46:00,440
Have you guys lost your minds,

725
00:46:00,520 --> 00:46:02,160
claiming that I'm Klao?

726
00:46:02,240 --> 00:46:04,480
Why then did you claim you were not Klao?

727
00:46:07,040 --> 00:46:08,560
Nobody here gets it.

728
00:46:08,640 --> 00:46:10,160
I told you I'm not Klao!

729
00:46:29,720 --> 00:46:31,360
Gosh, what the hell is going on?

730
00:46:33,080 --> 00:46:33,920
Master Klao!

731
00:46:36,720 --> 00:46:37,560
Master!

732
00:46:37,640 --> 00:46:38,520
Master Klao.

733
00:46:40,840 --> 00:46:41,680
Master Klao!

734
00:46:44,920 --> 00:46:45,800
<i>Where am I?</i>

735
00:46:45,880 --> 00:46:47,360
<i>How the hell did I end up here?</i>

736
00:46:47,440 --> 00:46:49,080
<i>What happened to me?</i>

737
00:46:49,640 --> 00:46:50,480
Master! Stop!

738
00:46:50,560 --> 00:46:51,480
Master.

739
00:46:51,560 --> 00:46:53,200
I beg you, Master.

740
00:46:54,640 --> 00:46:55,560
Wait, Master!

741
00:46:55,640 --> 00:46:56,480
Master Klao!

742
00:47:05,080 --> 00:47:06,280
Gosh! Still following me?

743
00:47:07,040 --> 00:47:07,880
Master Klao!

744
00:47:09,520 --> 00:47:11,640
<i>I must be in a film shoot</i>
<i>for a period piece.</i>

745
00:47:11,720 --> 00:47:14,240
<i>The extras are rehearsing</i>
<i>for their scenes.</i>

746
00:47:19,640 --> 00:47:21,040
Master!

747
00:47:21,120 --> 00:47:22,800
Please wait, Master.

748
00:47:22,880 --> 00:47:23,880
Master Klao.

749
00:47:23,960 --> 00:47:25,120
How is this even played?

750
00:47:26,640 --> 00:47:27,600
Master Klao!

751
00:47:27,680 --> 00:47:28,680
Hey, move!

752
00:47:29,200 --> 00:47:31,120
Out of the way!

753
00:47:31,200 --> 00:47:32,400
Move!

754
00:47:33,240 --> 00:47:34,120
Master…

755
00:47:34,200 --> 00:47:35,920
<i>Awesome job on the props.</i>

756
00:47:36,000 --> 00:47:37,480
<i>So realistic.</i>

757
00:47:37,560 --> 00:47:39,560
<i>What company is behind this?</i>

758
00:47:40,320 --> 00:47:41,440
Master Klao.

759
00:47:45,560 --> 00:47:46,560
Be wary, Master!

760
00:47:46,640 --> 00:47:47,480
Make way, please.

761
00:47:48,160 --> 00:47:49,720
Make way, I beg you!

762
00:47:49,800 --> 00:47:51,200
Please wait, Master.

763
00:47:53,080 --> 00:47:54,400
Yes, this is it!

764
00:47:54,480 --> 00:47:58,120
Many period pieces were filmed here!

765
00:48:01,640 --> 00:48:03,000
Where are all the crew?

766
00:48:03,080 --> 00:48:04,400
Help me!

767
00:48:05,600 --> 00:48:06,600
Master Klao!

768
00:48:07,360 --> 00:48:08,560
Do wait, Master!

769
00:48:10,880 --> 00:48:12,160
Do not go there!

770
00:48:12,240 --> 00:48:13,640
My feet can go no further!

771
00:48:14,600 --> 00:48:16,200
My poor feet can bear no more!

772
00:48:16,280 --> 00:48:18,280
-Master!
-This place is off-limits.

773
00:48:19,360 --> 00:48:20,760
This quarter is off-limits!

774
00:48:20,840 --> 00:48:22,080
Master.

775
00:48:22,160 --> 00:48:23,080
I beg of you, stop!

776
00:48:27,440 --> 00:48:28,760
Excuse me.

777
00:48:28,840 --> 00:48:30,840
You guys are working on a series, correct?

778
00:48:30,920 --> 00:48:32,120
Well…

779
00:48:32,960 --> 00:48:34,840
I'm not here to interrupt you, but…

780
00:48:36,680 --> 00:48:41,280
Can anyone tell me
how to get out of this filming location?

781
00:48:46,840 --> 00:48:47,840
Dear Klao.

782
00:48:48,840 --> 00:48:50,000
Where have you been to?

783
00:48:54,000 --> 00:48:55,320
Dearest Klao.

784
00:48:57,400 --> 00:48:58,720
So you have returned.

785
00:48:58,800 --> 00:49:00,520
Come, let us eat together.

786
00:49:03,840 --> 00:49:05,640
No, thank you.

787
00:49:06,800 --> 00:49:07,880
My Prayong.

788
00:49:08,600 --> 00:49:09,680
Yes, my love?

789
00:49:11,080 --> 00:49:12,840
Has dearest Klao lost his wits?

790
00:49:16,320 --> 00:49:18,120
Oh, good heavens.

791
00:49:18,640 --> 00:49:20,640
Indeed, a most unfortunate fate…

792
00:49:24,440 --> 00:49:25,280
Klao.

793
00:49:25,360 --> 00:49:26,760
Klao!

794
00:49:27,680 --> 00:49:28,600
Klao!

795
00:49:28,680 --> 00:49:30,400
-Settle this matter.
-Gosh!

796
00:49:30,480 --> 00:49:31,920
Stop chasing me!

797
00:49:38,840 --> 00:49:40,000
Oh, heavens!

798
00:49:40,080 --> 00:49:40,920
I'm really sorry!

799
00:49:42,560 --> 00:49:44,080
I nearly went down with him.

800
00:49:59,400 --> 00:50:01,680
<i>If this isn't a film set,</i>
<i>where the hell am I?</i>

801
00:50:01,760 --> 00:50:03,800
<i>Cross time travel off the list.</i>

802
00:50:05,400 --> 00:50:07,560
<i>And who the hell is that Lord Paddle Phop?</i>

803
00:50:07,640 --> 00:50:09,200
<i>It's not coming to me.</i>

804
00:50:09,280 --> 00:50:10,880
<i>But he looked at me</i>

805
00:50:10,960 --> 00:50:13,160
<i>like we'd known each other forever.</i>

806
00:50:14,360 --> 00:50:15,960
Master!

807
00:50:16,680 --> 00:50:18,000
Master Klao!

808
00:50:18,800 --> 00:50:20,800
Pray, stop running.

809
00:50:34,840 --> 00:50:35,680
Master Klao!

810
00:50:36,600 --> 00:50:38,240
At last, you are within my grasp!

811
00:50:38,320 --> 00:50:39,480
Remain still, Master.

812
00:50:40,360 --> 00:50:42,120
Be still, I beg you.

813
00:50:42,960 --> 00:50:44,840
Master Klao, cease this.

814
00:50:46,120 --> 00:50:47,200
Pray, remain still!

815
00:50:55,920 --> 00:50:57,400
Stop chasing me already!

816
00:50:58,760 --> 00:51:00,320
Help me, please.
Somebody, help.

817
00:51:01,400 --> 00:51:02,240
Klao!

818
00:51:03,440 --> 00:51:05,800
<i>Anyone but him!</i>

819
00:51:07,600 --> 00:51:09,080
Let us speak and be understood.

820
00:51:09,760 --> 00:51:11,040
I refuse!

821
00:51:11,120 --> 00:51:12,440
Oh, Master!

822
00:51:12,520 --> 00:51:14,120
Are you well?

823
00:51:21,560 --> 00:51:22,720
Sis, move!

824
00:51:31,120 --> 00:51:32,480
Gosh! My intrusive thoughts!

825
00:51:36,840 --> 00:51:38,120
<i>Everyone's acting so well.</i>

826
00:51:38,800 --> 00:51:40,920
<i>The artistic integrity is unreal.</i>

827
00:51:41,000 --> 00:51:43,400
<i>I don't think this is a film set.</i>

828
00:51:50,360 --> 00:51:52,280
What is the matter, Master Klao?

829
00:51:55,800 --> 00:51:56,960
<i>It hurts,</i>

830
00:51:57,040 --> 00:51:58,120
<i>but I'm not waking up.</i>

831
00:51:58,720 --> 00:52:00,400
<i>This isn't a dream.</i>

832
00:52:04,440 --> 00:52:07,280
<i>I don't think scammers</i>
<i>can pull off anything this fancy.</i>

833
00:52:07,360 --> 00:52:08,320
<i>Where am I even?</i>

834
00:52:08,400 --> 00:52:09,720
<i>A mysterious village</i>

835
00:52:09,800 --> 00:52:12,080
<i>with weird cultists, like in the movies?</i>

836
00:52:17,200 --> 00:52:18,040
Master Klao!

837
00:52:18,120 --> 00:52:19,480
Master!

838
00:52:19,560 --> 00:52:20,480
Cease this, Master.

839
00:52:20,560 --> 00:52:21,720
Master!

840
00:52:21,800 --> 00:52:22,640
A rooster!

841
00:52:22,720 --> 00:52:24,120
-Master!
-I am utterly weary.

842
00:52:25,000 --> 00:52:25,840
Master Klao!

843
00:52:27,400 --> 00:52:29,480
Master, where are you going?

844
00:52:33,720 --> 00:52:35,160
Master, I beg you!

845
00:52:35,240 --> 00:52:37,040
-Master Klao!
-I do fight back.

846
00:52:40,480 --> 00:52:42,040
Master, compose yourself!

847
00:52:42,960 --> 00:52:44,200
Be wary!

848
00:52:44,280 --> 00:52:45,320
I beg you, Master!

849
00:52:49,440 --> 00:52:51,920
-Don't come closer!
-Master, do cease this.

850
00:52:54,800 --> 00:52:56,120
What the hell are you?

851
00:52:57,200 --> 00:52:58,920
Do not go, I beg you!

852
00:53:00,080 --> 00:53:01,480
-Master!
-After him!

853
00:53:01,560 --> 00:53:02,480
Help me!

854
00:53:02,560 --> 00:53:03,960
-Master!
-Master Klao…

855
00:53:16,280 --> 00:53:17,320
Hey, stop!

856
00:53:22,080 --> 00:53:23,880
Hey! Don't come closer!

857
00:53:23,960 --> 00:53:25,520
I'll curse you…

858
00:53:25,600 --> 00:53:26,800
I'll curse you all!

859
00:53:26,880 --> 00:53:28,040
What do I do now?

860
00:53:28,120 --> 00:53:29,880
Espresso Petroleum!

861
00:53:29,960 --> 00:53:31,320
A perfect name for a drink.

862
00:53:52,320 --> 00:53:54,040
<i>Have I really traveled back in time?</i>

863
00:53:54,760 --> 00:53:56,080
<i>How did I even do it?</i>

864
00:53:57,320 --> 00:54:00,120
<i>When we think of traveling through time,</i>

865
00:54:03,320 --> 00:54:06,280
<i>we usually imagine it happening</i>
<i>with a time machine,</i>

866
00:54:06,360 --> 00:54:09,400
magic, some kind of sorcery,

867
00:54:10,400 --> 00:54:12,480
or a portal.

868
00:54:12,560 --> 00:54:17,560
<i>But sometimes, drifting off to sleep,</i>

869
00:54:17,640 --> 00:54:19,200
passing out,

870
00:54:19,800 --> 00:54:21,760
or being knocked out by an accident,

871
00:54:21,840 --> 00:54:24,840
can make someone travel back in time.

872
00:54:24,920 --> 00:54:27,080
When it comes to traveling back in time,

873
00:54:27,160 --> 00:54:30,840
death is considered the starting point.

874
00:54:30,920 --> 00:54:35,360
<i>It's about dying</i>
<i>and traveling to a different realm,</i>

875
00:54:35,440 --> 00:54:38,200
<i>then being reincarnated as someone else.</i>

876
00:54:39,480 --> 00:54:40,840
<i>A portal?</i>

877
00:54:42,360 --> 00:54:43,560
<i>Like in video games.</i>

878
00:54:43,640 --> 00:54:46,040
<i>If we die,</i>
<i>we'd start over from the beginning.</i>

879
00:54:46,120 --> 00:54:47,720
<i>I must've blacked out</i>

880
00:54:47,800 --> 00:54:49,000
<i>and ended up here.</i>

881
00:54:49,600 --> 00:54:50,920
<i>If I die now,</i>

882
00:54:51,000 --> 00:54:53,200
<i>do I go back to the present day?</i>

883
00:54:54,320 --> 00:54:55,200
My Lord…

884
00:54:55,800 --> 00:54:57,000
It has been far too long.

885
00:54:59,040 --> 00:55:00,160
At your word, shall we…

886
00:56:02,800 --> 00:56:04,080
This way, Curer.

887
00:56:07,160 --> 00:56:08,040
Thee!

888
00:56:08,120 --> 00:56:09,160
<i>Klao.</i>

889
00:56:09,240 --> 00:56:11,600
Pun! Yes. I'm safe now.

890
00:56:11,680 --> 00:56:14,200
Klao. Jom was right.
You lost your wits.

891
00:56:14,280 --> 00:56:15,320
<i>You…</i>

892
00:56:15,400 --> 00:56:18,800
<i>Your heart is more troubled</i>
<i>by Klao's affairs than your own.</i>

893
00:56:18,880 --> 00:56:20,120
That deadpan lord.

894
00:56:20,200 --> 00:56:21,200
<i>Is he taken?</i>

895
00:56:21,280 --> 00:56:24,840
<i>The Lord usually has no regard</i>
<i>for the welfare of others.</i>

896
00:56:25,560 --> 00:56:27,600
His concern is reserved solely for…

897
00:56:28,440 --> 00:56:29,400
<i>you, Master Klao.</i>
